bridge.js ports the native element arena, scoped view contexts, retained
callbacks and scheduler contract used by that prelude.
Core module export and component registration follows
crates/shell/src/engine/quickjs/mod.rs and
crates/shell/src/component_registry.rs at the same revision.

The port preserves sandbox.rs watchdog budgets: detached execution 10 seconds,
events and tasks 5 seconds, render and layout 2 seconds. Compilation uses the
same enclosing execution deadline. Render promise jobs drain on the next owner
turn, outside the render pass, as scheduler.rs requires.

On November 10, 2026 the user authorized replacing the JavaScript engine with
github.com/MoeForge/moejs v0.1.0. The engine's fixed MaxCallDepth=4096 in
engine/function.go bounds recursion with a RangeError. It is not configurable,
and no byte equivalence with QuickJS's stack setting is claimed.

As in sandbox.rs, the desktop runtime sets no heap ceiling. Host-retained
promises and temporary values are registered with AddLiveRoots, and owner turns
use RebaseAllocation, so a future authorized memory limit also counts retained
JavaScript. Values follow Go lifetime rather than QuickJS reference counting.
The pinned prelude does not mutate shared intrinsics, so their default frozen
state is preserved.
